# WHAT THE IMAGE BUILD MUST NOT CARRY. `docker/native.Dockerfile` compiles the binary itself, so it
# does `COPY . .` and everything not listed here is sent to the daemon on every build. A checkout
# that has been built once holds hundreds of megabytes of `build/` directories against ~30 MB of
# everything else, and CI never notices — a fresh checkout has none of them, which is exactly why
# this file is easy to forget and only bites on a developer's machine.
#
# NOTHING GIT TRACKS MAY BE LISTED HERE, and that is not tidiness. As far as git is concerned the
# build context is a working tree: the `io.github.youndie.kore.build` plugin runs git in it to
# decide the `dirty` flag it compiles into `/version`, and a tracked file excluded here reads as a
# deleted one — so the stamp says `-dirty` forever, from a clean checkout. A flag that is always on
# is a flag that says nothing. Everything below is in `.gitignore` already, and the list should stay
# that way.
#
# `.git` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT from this list: without it the commit in `/version` is `unknown`.
**/build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
.idea/
local.properties
.DS_Store
